The long run was not memory-bound; it was caused by recursive proof functions marked for aggressive simplification, which made the simplifier keep unfolding the symbolic interval. I stopped that run cleanly and am narrowing the equations to ordinary function evaluation so circularity—not unbounded simplifier expansion—handles the recursion.
